<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Rag.NET.Benchmarks.Quality</RootNamespace>
    <Description>Retrieval quality benchmark harness for Rag.NET: BEIR dataset loaders, native IR metrics and chunk-to-document aggregation</Description>
    <!-- A measurement harness, not a library anyone consumes: it exists so `dotnet build
         Rag.NET.slnx` compiles it and RepoConventions can see it, not so it ships. Phase 4.1 packs
         what the solution lists, and a nDCG calculator on nuget.org under the Rag.NET name would be
         a support surface nobody asked for. -->
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <VerifiedBy>unit</VerifiedBy>
    <!-- Milestone 6, Phase 6.2 §2(e). This is the measurement harness, so "exercise it against
         something real" is circular — it is the thing that does the exercising. Its correctness is
         established the only way a harness's can be: by agreement with published figures it did not
         author. BeirReproduction pins four of them at ±0.005 (SciFact 0.64593 among them), and
         every defect ever found in the dense path was found BY that agreement failing, not by a
         test of this package. That is a stronger check than any run of the harness against itself
         would be, and it is why the level stays unit rather than climbing to benchmark: the
         benchmark level means a package was measured by this harness, and this harness cannot
         measure itself. -->
    <VerifiedByReason>The measurement harness itself; it cannot be exercised against itself without circularity. Its correctness is the four-dataset parity agreement pinned in BeirReproduction at ±0.005, which is what has actually caught every defect in the dense path.</VerifiedByReason>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <AssemblyAttribute Include="System.Runtime.CompilerServices.InternalsVisibleToAttribute">
      <_Parameter1>Rag.NET.Benchmarks.Quality.Tests</_Parameter1>
    </AssemblyAttribute>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
